<ontology/use_hats_brushes_upholstery/use_hats_brushes_upholstery__0225__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 265" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n265> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Bristles used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: J. R. McCulloch, Dictionary of Commerce and Commercial Navigation (1880), scan p. 265"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BRISTLES: (Fr. soies; Ger. borsten; Dutch, borstels; Ital. setole; Span. cerdas, setas; Pol. szeczyny; Russ. schtschetina; Lat. setæ). The strong glossy hairs growing on the back of the hog and the wild boar. These are very extensively used by brushmakers, shoemakers, saddlers &c. and form a considerable article of import. British bristles are not to be had,..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
